Title: 0012-aros-volume-path-before-realpath
Repository: pragtical
Base-Commit: 5c05f09e081833b581fb5ecd10e64963dec87f03
Requires: 0011-aros-directory-notification.patch
Author: aros-pragtical project
Date: 2026-11-15
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS only, src/api/system.c f_absolute_path. Mainline x86_64 already returned the name unchanged in this case.

Problem:
  On ABIv11 a file given as a volume path (RAM:work/file) while the current directory is elsewhere was neither loaded nor saved: the C library's realpath() takes the name for a relative one and returns '<current directory>./RAM:work/file', and system.absolute_path accepted that result.
Solution:
  Recognise a volume path (a colon before any slash) before calling realpath() and return it unchanged.
Validation:
  2026-11-15, AROS One 1.3: pragtical RAM:w/proj/pl.txt started from SYS: failed to load and save before, loads and saves after. Mainline nightly 20261113 and Raspberry Pi unchanged.
Removal:
  Permanent.

diff --git a/src/api/system.c b/src/api/system.c
index a07a1168..7fcce90a 100644
--- a/src/api/system.c
+++ b/src/api/system.c
@@ -836,6 +836,17 @@ static int f_absolute_path(lua_State *L) {
   return 1;
 #elif defined(__AROS__)
   char resolved[PATH_MAX];
+  /* A volume path ("RAM:work/file", "Work:") is already absolute. Decide
+   * that before realpath(): the ABIv11 C library takes such a name for a
+   * relative one and returns "<current directory>./RAM:work/file". */
+  {
+    const char *colon = strchr(path, ':');
+    const char *slash = strchr(path, '/');
+    if (colon && colon != path && (!slash || colon < slash)) {
+      lua_pushstring(L, path);
+      return 1;
+    }
+  }
   if (path[0] && realpath(path, resolved)) {
     lua_pushstring(L, resolved);
     return 1;
